A Million Miles Apart.lyrics:
{c: Verse 1}{bars:16}

Its not long ago a thought of you would bring me joy
Feels like yesterday a sunny spot a place to lay
White fluff on a stem a hunt for luck for little boy
Picnics on the rock a smokey fire, a place to play

{c: Chorus}{bars:8}

Why did it have to fall apart? Where did it all go wrong
You feel a million miles apart and old and broken down

{c: Solo}{bars:8}

{c: Verse 2}{bars:16}

Spent time yesterday the two of us just like before
Green Grass in the fields a dusty road so much appeal
Years gone by so close a thankful gem to file away
Please don’t leave me now I’ll get it right, Come back for more

{c: Chorus}{bars:8}

Why did it have to fall apart? Where did it all go wrong
You feel a million miles apart and old and broken down

{c: Solo}{bars:8}

